<!--Render Target Documentation — Customizer
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.Customizer-->
<rdoc:Customizer xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    OpenSCAD customizer section
  </is>
  <documentation>
    The customizer generator writes the OpenSCAD customizer section for block
    and set files.

    For each exposed property:

    - Variable declaration with default value
    - Inline comment with customizer dropdown syntax where it applies
    - Group comment /* [Group Name] */ for property groups

    The hidden section /* [Hidden] */ holds derived variables that combine
    customizer inputs before they are passed to the module. Internal module
    computations are never placed in the hidden section.

    Every hidden customizer variable starts with hlp_. The prefix is
    HIDDEN_CUSTOMIZER_PREFIX in the render target naming module. FqnNaming
    defines it. The value is hlp_. The same prefix covers every kind: the
    selected config (hlp_config), a recombined split, and a resolved
    NoneOr value.

    OpenSCAD customizer supports only flat primitives, plus a vector of
    numbers up to length 4. A union that matches a rule in
    com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.CustomizerRules is projected into
    customizer fields. The render target reads that catalog from the type
    registry. Axis rules are considered before sentinel rules. A union
    with no matching rule stays one variable.

    AxisVector matches a number type with AxisXY or AxisXYZ of that same
    number. Decimal and Integer qualify. The variable keeps the property
    name and is the full vector. A scalar is repeated. An { x, y } or
    { x, y, z } value is written in full. Boolean, text, and enum axes
    stay one variable, because the customizer does not show those vectors.
    There is no hidden variable.

        holeXYGridOffsetZ = [3.5, 3.5];
        holeXYZAxleThickness = [1, 1, 1];

    SentinelToggle matches a union of exactly two named alternatives: a
    constant sentinel and one flat value type. Type arguments on the value
    arm are ignored. checkboxSelects is sentinel or value. checkboxSuffix
    is appended to the property name. The value field keeps the property
    name. inactiveDefault is the SCAD literal of that field while the
    property holds the sentinel. The sentinel literal is the constant
    type's value, serialized like any other property value.

    The current rules are Auto | Decimal (checkbox suffix Auto, checked
    selects Auto, inactiveDefault 0), Boolean.False | Text, and
    Boolean.False | FilePath (checkbox suffix On, checked selects the
    text or the path, inactiveDefault "").

        recessDepthAuto = true;
        recessDepth = 0;
        /* [Hidden] */
        hlp_recessDepthResolved = recessDepthAuto ? "auto" : recessDepth;

        textOn = false;
        text = "";
        /* [Hidden] */
        hlp_textResolved = textOn ? text : false;

    The main call passes the hidden variable under the property name.
    A three-arm union, such as Auto | Decimal | AxisXYZ(Decimal), matches
    neither rule and stays one variable.

    suggestions — a dropdown comment from the property suggestions. Each
    suggestion instance is serialized to its SCAD literal:

        textColor = "#303D4E"; // [#303D4E, #EAC645, #58B99D]

    Optional labels may come from documentation on the suggestion instances.

    constraints — Min and Max map to customizer range metadata
    [min:step:max] when both bounds exist. See the BlockML constraints
    documentation for the constraint instances. Individual constraints may also
    inform editor range hints.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:Presets" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:Customizer>
